<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Someshvara I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1042">1042</a>–<a href="/years/1068">1068</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Ahavamalla</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Someshvara I, also called Ahavamalla, was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-chalukya-empire">Western Chalukya Empire</a> from 1042 to 1068. He made Kalyani his capital and fought a long series of wars with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a>, in which the Chola king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajadhiraja-chola">Rajadhiraja I</a> was killed at Koppam in 1054, but he was later defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virarajendra-chola">Virarajendra Chola</a> at Kudalasangamam. Suffering from an incurable illness, he drowned himself in the Tungabhadra in 1068.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/someshvara-i.jpg" alt="Someshvara I" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Western_Chalukyas_of_Kalyana_King_Somesvara_I_Trailokyamalla_1043-1068.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
